+# Zero to One
+
+A cozy, dependency-free startup simulator prototype. One founder, one little office, and the first steps toward something bigger.
+
+## Run locally
+
+Requires **Node.js 18 or newer**. No install step, API keys, or internet connection needed.
+
+```sh
+cd /Users/michaelyang/Documents/projects/AIM/StartupSimulator
+npm start
+```
+
+Open **http://localhost:3000**. Stop the server with `Ctrl+C`.
+
+To choose another port: `PORT=3001 npm start`. The server binds to the loopback interface only. `npm run dev` restarts the server when its source changes; refresh the browser to see frontend changes.
+
+## Play
+
+- **Click or tap the floor** to walk there. The founder routes around furniture.
+- **Click furniture** to walk over and explore it. Coffee, the planning board, and your workstation advance the first-day checklist.
+- **WASD / arrow keys** move in screen directions. Movement slides along obstacles where possible.
+- **Space** pauses/resumes when focus is not on a button. **Escape** closes dialogs, cancels a walk, or resumes a paused game.
+- The **essentials buttons** and checklist offer keyboard-accessible destinations. Navigate with `Tab`, activate with `Enter` or `Space`.
+- **+/−** change the zoom; click the percentage to reset the view.
+- Sound is optional and off by default. The speaker button enables gentle, synthesized interaction sounds.
+- Coffee and couch breaks restore energy. Work uses 12 energy.
+- Position, energy, clock, checklist, and sound preference save to this browser’s local storage. The reset button asks for confirmation before replacing progress. If storage is unavailable, the game still works for the current session.
+
+This is intentionally a **single-office, day-one prototype**. There is no revenue simulation, hiring, office editing, or day progression yet. Time advances one in-game minute per three active seconds, with extra time for activities, and caps at 5:59 PM on day one. Dialogs, pause, and hidden tabs stop the clock. Walking does not consume energy, so the founder can always reach a break spot.
+
+## Checks
+
+```sh
+npm test
+npm run test:browser
+```
+
+The unit tests use Node’s built-in test runner and cover projection, collision boundaries, obstacle routing, connectivity between all objects, corrupted saves, and the static server.
+
+The browser smoke test uses a locally installed Chrome/Chromium in headless mode, with no additional dependencies. Set `CHROME_PATH` if Chrome is installed in a nonstandard location. It tests real canvas clicks, movement, furniture interactions, progress, save/reload, pause, keyboard input, zoom, reset, and mobile overflow. Screenshots are written to the temporary directory reported by the test.
+
+## Project layout
+
+- `server.js` — local-only static server; serves only the `public` directory.
+- `public/index.html`, `public/styles.css` — responsive UI, accessible controls and native dialogs.
+- `public/js/world.js` — office layout, collision geometry, A* pathfinding, save validation.
+- `public/js/renderer.js` — procedural isometric Canvas artwork, hit testing, animation and camera.
+- `public/js/game.js` — input, movement loop, interactions, checklist, audio and persistence.
+- `tests/` — unit/integration tests and the real-browser smoke test.
+
+All visuals are original procedural artwork. All fonts use the operating system’s local font stack. The app makes no external requests and collects no analytics.
